we are in the town of san jose in the  nagat province  everywhere we look there is devastation  this coastal community has been  completely damaged by typhoon rai we've  spoken to residents who are now forced  to sleep by the roadside because their  homes have been completely destroyed  we've been told we were the first  journalists to ever visit this community  a community that remains cut off from  the rest of the world there is debris  everywhere and people are forced to just  pick up the pieces they say they have  yet to see any government official they  have yet to receive any aid whatsoever  and the situation is quite desperate but  what we're seeing is just a fraction of  the devastation brought about by typhoon  rice fury there are at least five  provinces deeply affected by this  typhoon affecting millions of people the  government says it is doing the best it  can to send aid to those who need it  most especially those who live in  islands like this one but we spoke to  people here who say they are very  disappointed about the government  response and they feel abandoned and  they say even though they can't pick up  the pieces it's not going to be easy  because it also means that it will take  many many months before they can even  feel a semblance of normalcy again
 

